{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Patel, one of the hospitalists. You came in because of dark-brown drainage from your G-tube. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up around 4:30 this morning and noticed the fluid in the bag was dark brown, almost reddish. It’s usually greenish-yellow. I’ve had bleeding before, so I got worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good call. We checked a sample in the ER and it was guaiac positive, which means there’s blood. You’re on Lovenox for your history of blood clots—this could make bleeding more likely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I’ve been on Lovenox for my upper arm clots. But I don’t feel dizzy or weak. My blood pressure should be okay, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your vitals are stable—blood pressure 116/82, heart rate 93. We drew blood, and your hemoglobin was 10.2, which is a bit low but not a big drop from your baseline. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring. But why is this happening now? I had an EGD not too long ago and they said everything looked okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did. The last one showed some irritation and redness around the G-tube site, but no active bleeding. We think this might be related to that irritation, possibly worsened by the anticoagulant."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a new ulcer or something serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not that we know yet. The GI team wants to do another endoscopy to make sure. We’ll schedule that for tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my TPN? I haven’t had it since this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding TPN for now since we’re checking for bleeding. Nutrition team is involved, and you’ll restart it at home with your usual 12-hour cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my pain? I’ve been off morphine at home, but my belly’s been sore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you some IV Dilaudid for breakthrough pain, but we’re not continuing it after discharge. You’re still on gabapentin and amitriptyline, which help with nerve pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. I don’t want to get dependent again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We respect that. Also, social work mentioned you had some thoughts about not wanting to go on. Can you talk about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was overwhelmed in the ER. With everything—the pain, the bleeding, the tubes. I said things I didn’t mean. I’m not suicidal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad to hear that. Psychiatry saw you and agreed you’re safe. We’ll keep monitoring, but you’re cleared for regular care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2183-12-16 11:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just need to get through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2183-12-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Quick update—we ran blood cultures and they came back with no growth. No sign of infection in your bloodstream."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2183-12-16 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. What about that Enterococcus infection from my femoral line? Am I still on antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2183-12-16 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You completed the daptomycin course. Infectious disease reviewed it and said no further IV antibiotics are needed. You’ll keep the vancomycin lock for the line, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2183-12-16 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s one less thing to worry about."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2183-12-16 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture showed Streptococcus anginosus. It’s likely a contaminant or low-grade UTI, but since you’re not running a fever or feeling sick, we’re not treating it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2183-12-16 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be concerned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2183-12-16 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. We’ll watch it, but it’s probably not related to your current issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2183-12-17 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your repeat blood work shows your hemoglobin is stable at 10.9. No further drop. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2183-12-17 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. When’s the endoscopy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2183-12-17 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Scheduled for 9 a.m. You’ll be sedated, and the doctor will look for the source of the bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The endoscopy is done. Good news—no active bleeding. There’s mild gastritis around the G-tube site, and some old blood, but nothing urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s just irritation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We think the G-tube is causing some chronic irritation, and the Lovenox may have triggered a small bleed. But it’s healed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need a new tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. The site looks clean, no infection. We’ll keep monitoring. You’ll go back to your regular ranitidine—no PPIs due to your allergy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, omeprazole gave me kidney issues before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2183-12-17 10:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Ranitidine should help reduce stomach acid and protect the lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2183-12-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2183-12-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. The pain’s manageable. G-tube output is still brown, but less than before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2183-12-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. It’ll clear over the next few days as the old blood drains out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2183-12-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my Lovenox? Should I stop it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2183-12-18 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’re keeping it. Your history of upper extremity clots is serious. The benefit outweighs the small bleeding risk, especially now that the bleeding has stopped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2183-12-18 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll keep using it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2183-12-18 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’ll go home with your regular medications and restart TPN with home health support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2183-12-18 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No changes to my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2183-12-18 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "None. Same doses of gabapentin, amitriptyline, ranitidine, levothyroxine, and the rest. You’ll also keep the vancomycin lock for your line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2183-12-18 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Dilaudid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2183-12-18 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not sending it home with you. Use your oral morphine if needed, but try the other pain meds first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2183-12-18 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2183-12-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Your condition is stable, no active bleeding, and your labs are consistent with your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2183-12-19 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2183-12-19 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your home health team to restart TPN. If the G-tube output becomes bright red or you feel lightheaded, go to the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2183-12-19 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2183-12-19 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—you had a small bowel endoscopy today as part of your evaluation. It was unremarkable, no source of bleeding found beyond the mild stomach irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So everything’s okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. This was likely a small, self-limited bleed from G-tube irritation. With your history, we wanted to be thorough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll document everything for your follow-up team. You’re cleared to leave once the discharge papers are ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep an eye on your mood. If you feel overwhelmed again, please reach out. You’re not alone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m feeling much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with your discharge instructions and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also reviewed your hepatitis C—it’s stable, no liver issues now. Continue your usual monitoring with your specialist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have an appointment next month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2183-12-19 12:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Stay on track with that."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2183-12-16 11:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2183-12-19 14:21:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman with a complex medical history including sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic G-tube and TPN dependence, and a history of upper extremity DVTs was admitted for dark-brown G-tube output concerning for gastrointestinal bleeding. She had been on Lovenox for anticoagulation and had a history of prior GI bleeds. Initial evaluation showed guaiac-positive drainage and stable hemoglobin. An endoscopy revealed mild G-tube-related gastritis with no active bleeding, and a small bowel endoscopy was unremarkable. Blood cultures showed no growth, and a urine culture grew Streptococcus anginosus, which was not treated due to lack of symptoms. She was not on IV antibiotics as her recent Enterococcus avium line infection had been completed. Suicidal ideation expressed in the ED was evaluated and cleared by psychiatry. She remained on home medications including ranitidine, anticoagulation, and pain management with gabapentin and amitriptyline. TPN was held during admission and planned for restart at home. She was discharged home with services, stable and with no active bleeding.",
    "problems": [
      "Hemorrhage of gastrointestinal tract, unspecified",
      "Other gastrostomy complications",
      "Surgical operation with formation of external stoma causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Duodenitis, without mention of hemorrhage",
      "Suicidal ideation"
    ]
  }
}
